# QUESTION : STATEFUL vs STATELESS ARCHITECTURE ?
=====================================================

Pichle chapter (Scaling) me humne dekha ki Horizontal Scaling ke baad application ke multiple instances run karte hain.

Ab agar user ki session information kisi ek server ki RAM me stored ho, to Load Balancer next request kisi doosre server par bhej sakta hai — jiske paas wo session information nahi hogi.

Isi problem ko samajhne ke liye hume Stateful aur Stateless Architecture samajhna hoga.


--------------------------------
## QUESTION : STATE KYA HAI ?
--------------------------------

State simply means information that a system remembers and uses while processing future requests.


-----------------------------------
## QUESTION : STATELESS KYA HAI ?
-----------------------------------

Stateless application previous requests ki information (state) remember nahi karti.

Har request independently process hoti hai, aur us request ko process karne ke liye
required saari information usi request ke saath aati hai.


-----------------------------------
## QUESTION : STATEFUL KYA HAI ?
-----------------------------------

A Stateful application previous requests ki information (state) ko remember karti hai aur future
requests ko process karte time usi stored information ka use karti hai.


------------------------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION : STATE MAINTAIN KARNE KI ZARURAT KYUN PADTI HAI ?
------------------------------------------------------------------

HTTP protocol by default Stateless hota hai. Matlab server ko previous requests yaad nahi rehti.

Lekin real-world applications me user ko har request par dobara login karwana practical nahi hai.

Isliye applications ko kisi mechanism ki zarurat hoti hai jo multiple HTTP / HTTPS requests ke beech 
user-related information maintain kar sake.

Traditional Java web applications is purpose ke liye HttpSession use karti hain.





=====================================
# QUESTION : WHAT IS HTTP SESSION ?
=====================================

HTTP / HTTPS (HTTP + TLS/SSL) protocol by default stateless hota hai.

Matlab server ko by default ye yaad nahi rehta ki:
    - Current request kis user ne bheji hai
    - Us user ne isse pehle koi request bheji thi ya nahi

Lekin real-world applications me hume user ki kuch information
multiple requests ke beech maintain karni padti hai.

HttpSession ek server-side object hai jo Servlet Container (e.g., Tomcat)
provide karta hai. Ye user/client se related temporary information ko
multiple HTTP requests ke beech maintain karta hai.


----------------------------------
## LOGIN-BASED APPLICATIONS ME :
----------------------------------

Application (e.g., Spring Security) pehle user ko authenticate karti hai
(i.e. verify karti hai ki username/password ya other credentials valid hain).

Authentication successful hone ke baad:
    - Application Servlet Container (e.g., Tomcat) se HttpSession create karwati hai
    - HttpSession me user-related temporary information store hoti hai
    - Ye information subsequent HTTP/HTTPS requests ko process karne me use hoti hai

Isi HttpSession ki help se baad wali requests me user ko identify kiya jaata hai
(Authentication Context), aur uske Roles/Permissions ke basis par
Authorization perform ki ja sakti hai.


