## NOTE:
----------

1: Technically Shopping Cart jaise business data ko HttpSession
   me store kiya ja sakta hai, lekin modern distributed applications
   generally aisa avoid karti hain.

   Business data (Cart, Wishlist, Orders, etc.) usually Database
   me store hota hai, jabki HttpSession sirf temporary user context
   (e.g. Logged-in User, Roles, Authentication Status) maintain
   karne ke liye use hota hai.

   Isliye HttpSession expire hone, server restart/crash hone ke baad bhi important business data available rehta hai.


2: HttpSession khud koi storage technology (jaise Redis, Database, ya File System) nahi hai.
   Ye sirf ek server side Session Object hai.
   By default, Tomcat jaise Servlet Containers is Session Object ko server ki local memory (RAM) me store karte hain.


3. HttpSession sirf authenticated users ke liye limited nahi hai.
   Anonymous (non-logged-in) users ke liye bhi HttpSession
   use kiya ja sakta hai.

   Example:

    Anonymous User
          ↓
    Add Product to Cart
          ↓
    HttpSession
          ↓
    Temporary Cart

Baad me jab user login karta hai, to application us temporary cart ko user ke account se associate karke Database me persist kar deti hai.



