## QUESTION : KYA HTTP SESSION EXPIRE HOTI HAI? YA USER LIFETIME LOGIN REHTA HAI?
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Haan, HttpSession expire hoti hai. User lifetime login nahi rehta.

Generally session in situations me end hoti hai:


1. SESSION TIMEOUT (MOST COMMON)
---------------------------------

Agar user configured timeout period (e.g. 30 minutes) tak koi request nahi bhejta, to Tomcat automatically HttpSession destroy kar deta hai.

Spring Boot Configuration:

server.servlet.session.timeout=30m


2. USER LOGOUT
---------------

Jab user logout karta hai, application session.invalidate() call karke current HttpSession ko immediately destroy kar deti hai.


3. SERVER RESTART
------------------

By default HttpSession server ki local memory (RAM) me store hoti hai. Server restart hone par RAM clear ho jaati hai, aur saari HttpSessions destroy ho jaati hain.


4. SERVER CRASH
----------------

Server crash hone par RAM me stored saari HttpSessions lost ho jaati hain. Result: user ko dobara login karna padta hai.



