## QUESTION : SPRING BOOT ME COMPLETE JWT AUTHENTICATION FLOW KAISE KAAM KARTA HAI?
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose humare paas ek Spring Boot application hai
jo JWT-based authentication use karti hai.


### LOGIN FLOW :
------------------


STEP 1: LOGIN ENDPOINT BANANA
-------------------------------

Developer ek login endpoint banata hai:

POST /api/auth/login



STEP 2: LOGIN REQUEST SPRING BOOT APPLICATION TAK PAHUNCHTI HAI
-----------------------------------------------------------------

User credentials enter karta hai:

username = anurag
password = ******

Client request bhejta hai:

POST /api/auth/login
{
"username": "anurag",
"password": "password123"
}


Ab ye request directly Controller tak nahi jaati. Spring Boot application me request sabse pehle Spring Security Filter Chain se pass hoti hai.

Filter Chain check karti hai: "Kya is endpoint ke liye authentication required hai?"

- Agar endpoint permitAll() hai → Filter Chain request ko aage pass kar deti hai → Controller tak pahunchti hai
- Agar endpoint authenticated() hai → Filter Chain pehle verify karti hai ki request authenticated user se aayi hai ya nahi → tab Controller tak pahunchti hai


Login endpoint ko normally permitAll() kiya jata hai, taaki user login karne ke liye pehle se authenticated hona na pade. 
Baaki sab endpoints authenticated() hote hain.


#### CODE SNIPPET:
-------------------

