@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {
   @Bean
   SecurityFilterChain securityFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
      http.authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
         .requestMatchers("/api/auth/login").permitAll()
         .anyRequest().authenticated()
     );

     return http.build();
   }  
}



STEP 3: CONTROLLER REQUEST KO SERVICE LAYER KO DELEGATE KARTA HAI
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Controller request ko underlying service (e.g JwtService) ko delegate karta hai:

Ye separation of concerns follow karta hai:

- Controller → sirf HTTP request/response handle karta hai
- Service → actual authentication aur JWT generation logic handle karti hai



STEP 4: SERVICE CREDENTIALS KO AuthenticationManager KO DETI HAI
---------------------------------------------------------------------

AuthenticationManager authentication process ko appropriate AuthenticationProvider ko delegate karta hai. 

Username/password based authentication ke liye commonly DaoAuthenticationProvider use hota hai.

Different authentication mechanisms ke liye different AuthenticationProviders ho sakte hain:

Username/Password → DaoAuthenticationProvider
LDAP → LdapAuthenticationProvider
OAuth2/OIDC → OAuth2/OIDC-specific providers


