STEP 6: PasswordEncoder PASSWORD VERIFY KARTA HAI
---------------------------------------------------

Ab Spring Security ke paas: User Provided Password and DB Stored Password Hash available hain.


#### PASSWORD STORAGE:
-----------------------

  User ka password Database me plain-text form me store nahi kiya jata. Password ko store karne se
  pehle application PasswordEncoder.encode() ka use karke password ka hash generate karti hai, 
  aur us hash ko Database me store karti hai.


#### PASSWORD VERIFICATION
---------------------------

Login ke time:

        User enters:
        "password123"

             ↓

    PasswordEncoder.matches(
        "password123",
        $2a$10$....hashed-password
    )

             ↓

    Stored hash ko inspect karta hai
             ↓
    Usme se hashing algorithm + parameters + salt extract karta hai
             ↓
    Provided password ko SAME algorithm, SAME parameters aur SAME salt
    ke saath process karta hai
             ↓
    Result ko DB stored password hash se compare karta hai


#### NOTE: 
-----------

PasswordEncoder DB ka hash decrypt nahi karta — kyunki password hash generally one-way hota hai.



STEP 7: AUTHENTICATION OBJECT RETURN HOTA HAI
------------------------------------------------

#### Agar password valid hai:
-----------------------------

    Authentication Successful
            ↓
    AuthenticationProvider authenticated Authentication object return karta hai
            ↓
    AuthenticationManager usse Service ko return karta hai


