-----------------------------

Authentication Spring Security me ek interface hai jo authenticated user ko represent
karne ka contract provide karta hai.

Iske alag-alag concrete implementations use hote hain depending on use case:

- Login flow → UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken
- JWT verification → JwtAuthenticationToken
- Anonymous users → AnonymousAuthenticationToken


Authentication successful hone ke baad conceptually
isme information ho sakti hai:

    Authentication
       |
    UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken
       |
       ├── Principal
       |      └── UserDetails
       |             ├── username = anurag
       |             ├── userId = 101
       |             └── ...
       |
       ├── Authorities
       |      └── ROLE_USER
       |
       └── Authenticated
              └── true




STEP 8: JWT GENERATION
-------------------------

Authentication successful hone ke baad Service ke paas authenticated user 
ki information Authentication object ke through available hoti hai.

Technically Controller khud JWT generate nahi karta. Controller underlying
Service (e.g., JwtService) ko call karta hai, aur service authenticated
user ki information ke basis par JWT claims prepare karti hai,
token generate karti hai, aur usse Signing Key ke saath sign karti hai.

Uske baad Controller ko return kard deti hai, 
aur Controller usse client ko response me bhejta hai.



