## QUESTION : ACCESS TOKEN vs REFRESH TOKEN ?
----------------------------------------------

Agar JWT ko 30 days ka rakhein, to user ko baar-baar login nahi karna padega — convenient hai.
Lekin agar token leak/stolen ho gaya, to attacker usse 30 days tak misuse kar sakta hai. Security risk hai.

Agar JWT ko 5 minutes ka rakhein, to security better ho jaati hai — stolen token ka misuse window bahut chhota ho jaata hai.
Lekin ab user ko har 5 minutes ke baad dobara username/password daal kar login karna padega. Poor user experience.

Hume aisa mechanism chahiye jisme:

    - Security better rahe (stolen token ka misuse limited ho, i.e., token ki validity window kam rahe)
    - User experience bhi achha ho. (user ko baar-baar login na karna pade)


## SOLUTION :
---------------

Ek hi JWT se dono achieve karna possible nahi. Isliye do tokens use kiye jaate hain:

Login ke time authentication successful hone ke baad application do tokens issue karti hai:

Access Token + Refresh Token



### QUESTION : ACCESS TOKEN KYA HAI ?
---------------------------------------

Access Token ka primary purpose hai Protected APIs/Resources ko access karna.

Client API request ke saath Access Token bhejta hai:

GET /api/orders
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>

Application usse verify karke Authentication → Authorization perform karti hai, aur phir Allow/Reject decide karti hai.

#### IMPORTANT : 
-----------------

Access Token generally short-lived rakha jata hai — jaise 5, 15, ya 30 minutes. Exact duration application ki security requirements par depend karti hai.



### QUESTION : REFRESH TOKEN KYA HAI ?
----------------------------------------

Refresh Token ka use normal business APIs access karne ke liye nahi hota. 
Iska primary purpose hai — Access Token expire hone ke baad naya Access Token obtain karna.


#### FLOW :
------------

Access Token Expired
↓
Client Refresh Token ko designated token endpoint par bhejta hai
↓
Application Refresh Token validate karti hai
↓
Naya Access Token issue hota hai

Is process me user ko dobara username/password se login nahi karna padta.


Agar Refresh Token bhi expire ho gaya, to naya Access Token obtain nahi kiya ja sakta — user ko dobara login karna padega.
Yaani Refresh Token longer-lived login experience deta hai, lekin indefinitely valid nahi hota.


#### IMPORTANT : 
-----------------

- Refresh Token generally Access Token se longer-lived hota hai:

  Example:

   Access Token → 15 minutes
   Refresh Token → 30 days

- Access Token aur Refresh Token dono ka JWT hona mandatory nahi hai — dono kuch bhi ho sakte hain (JWT ya opaque token).
  Lekin practically Access Token generally JWT hota hai and Refresh Token commonly opaque hota hai 



### QUESTION : REFRESH TOKEN SE NEW ACCESS TOKEN KAISE MILTA HAI ?
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose:

Access Token Expiry = 1 hour
Refresh Token Expiry = 30 days

User login karta hai, aur successful authentication ke baad client ko backend se 
Access Token + Refresh Token milta hai. Client dono tokens ko securely store karta 
hai aur Access Token ko subsequent API requests me use karta hai.

Refresh Token khud automatically naya Access Token generate nahi karta. Client me 
logic implement kiya jaata hai jo decide karta hai ki naya Access Token kab obtain 
karna hai.

Client 2 situations me Refresh Token se naya Access Token obtain kar sakta hai:

- Approach 1: Jab Access Token expire hone wala ho (expiry se pehle).
              Is approach me Access Token expire hone se pehle hi new Access Token
              client ko available ho jata hai, isliye API requests me interruption nahi hota.

- Approach 2: Jab Access Token expire hone ke baad pehli request aaye 
              (401 Unauthorized milne par)

Dono cases me client Backend ke designated token endpoint par Refresh Token bhejta 
hai, application us Refresh Token ko validate karti hai, aur successful validation 
ke baad naya Access Token obtain karta hai, aur usse apne side store kar leta hai.



#### NOTE : 
------------

Refresh Token se naya Access Token issue hone par purana Access Token automatically invalidate nahi hota.

Agar purane token ki expiry abhi baaki hai, to wo apni expiry tak valid rehta hai — aur naya token bhi valid
hota hai (dono kuch time ke liye simultaneously valid).

Agar application revocation mechanism use karti hai, to old token ko explicitly invalidate kiya ja sakta hai.





